{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794308568,"nonce":"RWGyFeLfP1SA1T/uOswkIsr+zKg=","title":"A periodic multi-field Newton tangent falls onto the dense path","message":"reduce_matrix_periodic forms P^T J P inside the traced Newton body. For a multi-field reduction whose blocks are not all plain selections (an N1E tie next to a Lagrange tie), it needs the block-diagonal P. Only the slip builder cached it eagerly; the periodic builders did not, so inside the trace it could not be rebuilt and the reduction silently densified to n x n. The Dirichlet elimination after it then crashed ('DynamicJaxprTracer has no attribute data'). At 3-D sizes the dense path alone does not fit in memory. Fix in the working tree: every multi-field builder returns through _multifield_reduction, which caches P_blockdiag. Test: tests/test_fem_nonnodal_nonlinear_surface.py::test_a_periodic_multifield_tangent_stays_sparse_inside_the_newton_trace.","files":null}]}